# The nursemaid's specter in the nursery doorway (death_house_third). She can be calmed with the lullaby from the
# conservatory harpsichord, talked or prayed to rest, or fought (nursery_specter: one specter, 200 XP, level 1).

~ start
Narrator: A woman made of mist and cold hangs in the nursery doorway, her apron grey, her face worn down to the shape of worry. Her hands are cupped as if around a sleeping child.
durst_nursemaid [sad]: Have you brought him? Have you brought my Walter back up?
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Easy, madam. Easy now. We're not the ones who took him. We'd never.
-> choose

~ choose
* [if flag.death_house_knows_lullaby] Hum her the lullaby from the harpsichord. -> lullaby
* [Persuasion DC 14] Tell her Walter is gone and she can rest. If she won't believe it, she attacks. -> rest_ok | rest_fail
* [Cleric] [Religion DC 13] Pray her to rest, as for any mother. If the prayer fails, she attacks. -> rest_ok | rest_fail
* [Insight DC 12] What does she want, really? -> insight | insight_fail
* Strike first, before she does. -> fight
* Back away. -> END

~ insight
Narrator: She doesn't want revenge; she wants to hear him once more. She would know his song anywhere.
-> choose

~ insight_fail
Narrator: Grief, and cold, and something sharper under it. {name} can't tell which will win.
-> choose

~ lullaby
Narrator: {name} hums the first bar, a little off key, and the nursemaid goes very still. By the second bar she is humming too, and her cupped hands rock, and rock.
durst_nursemaid [sad]: He was mine. The master's and mine. The mistress gave him to the robed ones the night he was born, and they carried him down, and I followed them.
durst_nursemaid [sad]: He's under the house. He's been under the house so long. If you go down, sing it to him. Someone should.
Narrator: She rocks the empty air one last time and is gone, the way breath goes from a window.
-> calmed

~ rest_ok
Narrator: The words reach her slowly, like warmth into frozen hands. Her cupped hands open, and there is nothing in them, and she looks at the nothing for a long time.
durst_nursemaid [sad]: Gone. Yes. I knew. I knew when they stopped him crying. They stopped me too, at the bottom of the stairs.
Narrator: She fades from the doorway like a word you meant to say and didn't.
-> calmed

~ calmed
set death_house_nursemaid_calmed
if not flag.death_house_learned_walter
  set death_house_learned_walter
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Be at peace, sister. The dawn comes, even for you. Especially for you.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: I don't like this house. I'd like that in writing. Signed, and witnessed.
if not name:liriel_dawnsong
  interject class:cleric: Rest. You've earned it more than anyone in this house.
endif
-> END

~ rest_fail
durst_nursemaid [angry]: Liars. You're with them. You're wearing their faces!
-> fight

~ fight
Narrator: The cold comes off her like a slammed door.
combat nursery_specter
